# Build artifacts
/bin/
/dist/
# `make build` writes to bin/; a binary at the repo root is always a stray
# artifact from a manual `go build ./cmd/...` and must never be committed.
/lolstats-aggregate
/lolstats-ingest

# Verbose agent output and captured pages: evidence for a single task, not part
# of the project's history.
/.agent-artifacts/

# Scratch trees: drill output, before/after captures, working copies. Excluded
# by pattern rather than by name, because the cost of a miss is not symmetric -
# an unignored scratch tree is one `git add -A` away from entering project
# history, and a nested `git worktree` under the repository would be staged as a
# gitlink to a commit nothing references, which is a broken submodule entry
# rather than a recoverable mistake.
/files/
/.zz-*
/.lane-*

# Local data / secrets
.env
deploy/secret.yaml
*.pem
*.key

# Local planning notes, never shared/committed
/backlog.local.md

# IDE / OS
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
*.iml

# `make build` writes to `/bin/`. `build/` is different, and it is now empty:
# it held the Docker image *contexts* (`build/caddy`, `build/site`) until the
# static tier was deleted on 2026-09-17. This rule stays because a
# binary dropped there would sit in a directory that any future image context
# added back would send to the builder and bake into an image; a hand-rolled
# `go build` into that directory did exactly that once.
/build/lolstats-*

# `web/` was the retired Astro tree, deleted outright on 2026-09-18. These four
# rules stay even though the directory is gone: a rule for a deleted directory is
# a harmless no-op, whereas its absence is a live trap the moment anything
# recreates the path. The lesson is in the sequencing - an ignore rule may only be
# retired *with* the tree it protects, never before it.
#
# Note the root `/dist/` rule earlier in this file does NOT cover `web/dist`: it
# is anchored to the repository root.
/web/node_modules/
/web/dist/
/web/.astro/
/web/.vercel/

# Go
*.test
*.out
coverage.txt

# Python (used only for ad-hoc data inspection, never a dependency)
__pycache__/
